      "writtenOn": "2022-02-03T18:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the idea of requiring that the enum-name is eliminated if the Zephyr API is used.\n\nWith the EEPROM change, GPIO_WP_L is now only used in 2 places in the legacy code: flash.c and switch.c (plus some tests).  \n\nI think doing a minor refactor and creating a common/write_protect.c that provides write_protect_is_asserted().  This can then handle the CONFIG_WP_ACTIVE_HIGH for legacy code.  You can add a Zephyr file under zephyr/shim/src/write_protect.c that only uses Zephyr APIs.",
      "parentUuid": "f51a1b31_099cf610",
      "revId": "52a5aad42237416f7132f9474b9b0d0a220401d9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
